msgid "5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:0
msgid "`BUFFER_GLOBAL_LOAD`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:0
msgid "buffer loads to LDS and pre-gfx1250 global loads to LDS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:34
msgid ""
"Bits 4 and 6 through 10 are reserved for future async operations, and no "
"operation belongs to them yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:37
msgid ""
"Which async operations a given subtarget actually has is described in {ref}"
"`AMDGPU DMA Operations <amdgpu-dma-operations>`. A stage exists on every "
"subtarget that supports asyncmarks, whether or not that subtarget has any "
"operation belonging to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:42
msgid "Stage Masks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:44
msgid ""
"`asyncmark` intrinsics take a *stage mask*: an 11-bit value in which a set "
"bit names a stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:47
msgid ""
"The zero mask, which sets no bit, is given the special meaning \"every "
"stage\". This ensures if new stages are added that programs will continue to "
"wait on all stages, if that was their intention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:51
msgid ""
"Bits not specified in the table above are reserved for future use. It is not "
"an error to set them, but it could mean you have more conservative waits "
"than necessary when the future stages are added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:55
msgid ""
"Setting a bit that is neither listed nor reserved is an error, and is "
"rejected by the IR verifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:58
msgid ""
"[Informational note --- Since the stages are independent, any mix of masks "
"is valid. A program is easiest to reason about by considering the sequence "
"of each stage separately.]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:62
msgid "Current Sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:64
msgid ""
"The abstract machine maintains a separate sequence of asyncmarks *for each "
"stage* during the execution of a function body, which excludes any "
"asyncmarks produced by calls to other functions encountered in the currently "
"executing function. The state of the sequence for a stage `S` at each "
"program point in the function is called the *current sequence of* `S`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:70
msgid ""
"The sequences of distinct stages are independent: appending to one does not "
"affect the length or contents of any other, even though multiple sequences "
"may be appended to with a single call to asyncmark (by naming multiple "
"stages)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:74
msgid "`@llvm.amdgcn.asyncmark(i32 %K)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:76
msgid ""
"Appends an asyncmark to the current sequence of every stage named in the "
"mask `K`. The sequences of the stages that `K` does not name are unaffected. "
"`K` must be a constant stage mask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:80
msgid "`@llvm.amdgcn.wait.asyncmark(i16 %N, i32 %K)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:82
msgid ""
"For every stage named by the mask `K`, ensures that the length of the "
"current sequence of that stage is at most `N` by removing asyncmarks from "
"the start of that sequence if it is longer than `N`. The sequences of the "
"stages that `K` does not name are unaffected. `K` must be a constant stage "
"mask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:87
msgid "Completion of Asyncmarks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:89
msgid ""
"An asyncmark `M`, produced by an `asyncmark` operation `X`, is *completed-"
"at*  a `wait.asyncmark()` operation `Y` with mask `B` in the same function "
"body if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:92
msgid "`X` is *program-ordered* before `Y`, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:93
msgid "`B` names the stage of the sequence that `M` belongs to, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:94
msgid ""
"`M` is not in the current sequence at any operation `Z` that immediately "
"follows `Y` in *program-order*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:97
msgid "Completion of Async Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:99
msgid ""
"An async operation executes outside the thread that initiated it, i.e., it "
"is not related in *program-order* with any other operations from that "
"thread. But the thread can use an asyncmark to ensure that the async "
"operation is *completed-at* some later operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:104
msgid ""
"An async operation `A` *initiated-by* an instruction `I` is *completed-at* "
"some `wait.asyncmark()` operation `Y` with stage mask `B` if there exists an "
"`asyncmark()` operation `X` with mask `C`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:108
msgid "`I` is *program-ordered* before `X`, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:109
msgid "`I` belongs to a stage in `C`, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:110
msgid "`X` is *completed-at* `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:112
msgid "happens-before"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:114
msgid ""
"When an instruction `I` initiates an async operation `A`, `I` *happens-"
"before* `A`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:117
msgid ""
"If `A` is *completed-at* a `wait.asyncmark()` operation `Y`, then `A` "
"*happens-before* `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:120
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:122
msgid ""
"Most examples below use the zero mask, so every asyncmark tracks every async "
"operation and there is only one sequence to reason about. The {ref}"
"`interleaved stages <amdgpu-async-interleaved-stages>` example shows what "
"narrower masks add."
msgstr ""

