msgid ""
"A mask need not name just one stage. An asyncmark whose mask names several "
"is appended to each of their sequences, and a wait whose mask names several "
"trims each of them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:282
msgid "Implementation notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:284
msgid "[This section is informational.]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:286
msgid "Function Calls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:288
msgid ""
"In general, at a function call, if the caller uses sufficient waits to track "
"its own async operations, the actions performed by the callee cannot affect "
"correctness. But inlining such a call may result in redundant waits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:307
msgid ""
"Before inlining, it is unspecified whether `X` is *completed-at* `D`, while "
"`C` is **not** *completed-at* `D`. The programmer can only rely on `B` being "
"*completed-at* `D`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:322
msgid ""
"After inlining, `C` is also *completed-at* `D` and `X` is **not** *completed-"
"at* `D`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:325
msgid ""
"Conversely, a `wait.asyncmark` call inside a callee cannot be used to track "
"asyncmarks from the caller, since this `wait.asyncmark` can only observe the "
"current sequence of the callee."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:344
msgid ""
"In the above example, it is unspecified whether `B` and `C` in `bar()` are "
"*completed-at* `Y`, because they are not included in the sequence that can "
"be examined at `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:359
msgid "After inlining, both `B` and `C` are *completed-at* `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:361
msgid "Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:363
msgid ""
"The implementation may eliminate/modify asyncmark/wait intrinsics in the "
"following cases. These are just examples and not meant to be an exhaustive "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:366
msgid ""
"An `asyncmark` operation which remains in a current sequence along every "
"path that reaches the function exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:377
msgid ""
"Here, the zero mask names every stage, and each independent mark remains, so "
"the entire mark `X` can be eliminated. If only some sequences qualified, "
"then the `asyncmark` operation could be modified to remove just those stages "
"from its mask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:382
msgid ""
"A `wait.asyncmark` which sees an empty sequence of asyncmarks along every "
"path that reaches it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:393
msgid ""
"Here, as with `X` above, every sequence qualifies, so `Y` can be eliminated. "
"If only some sequences qualified, the `wait.asyncmark` could be modified to "
"only wait for the relevant stages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:397
msgid ""
"An `asyncmark` operation that has mask bits that don't refer to any "
"instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:409
msgid "Here, the program can be refined to -"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUAsyncOperations.md:420
msgid ""
"Since only that particular stage is actually relevant to ensuring the "
"completion of async operations."
msgstr ""
